I guess that regulars here have read this:

http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_thread/thread/0760e25393f22ba7#

OK, for several reasons I don't agree at all with rules. For my
standard, getting to the priest at XL1 with 3200$ is quite enough (I
routinely do it with 12000$, but that's less than guaranteed). The
rest of the rules are pretty lame. I could get the protection, hand
the keyboard to any half competent player, and there's no way he'll be
in a worse position than in turn 1. The loss of focus because of
previous PR style is lost, and I don't see any rules stating that team
playing is cheating in any way. So, if I get a 100% success in getting
the protection, I don't see why it's not a winning strategy.

The protection racket is most suitable with Healers, Tourists,
Knights, Archaeologists and Monks, so I used to play mostly those
characters. I got almost, but not quite, 100% success. Most failures
due to overdoing it (getting down to lvl10 at XL1 to find "just one
more shop", for example)

I got bored, so I started playing other characters at random. Not
quite the same succes rate. Just some 50%. Then I read about a couple
of tricks that I hadn't tested (digging in the mines beside my pet
instead of looking for the stairs, plus some improvements in the speed
and efficiency of shoplifting) Now I always succeed at the PR, with
any character at random. I only lose if I overdo it. If I am
conservative (only go down to lvl4), that's a 100% success rate. Well,
with nethack there's no such thing as 100% (you can always lose your
pet to a trap in turn 1) but you know what I mean...

So, in my opinion, nethack (without conducts) is a solved game, and PR
is a winning strategy.

BTW, has anyone studied Marvin's strategy? Or any other winning
strategy?


